.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt KLDINFO 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldinfo
.Nd show KLD module (.ko) file dependency and version information
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl rv
.Ar modname | Ar modpath | Ar kernel
.Op ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility parses ELF header of KLD
.Ar modname Ns Pa .ko ,
then searches for available Kernel Loadable objects and shows their dependency
and version information.
If pathname
.Ar modpath
is given, the utility tries to open it directly, it quits if open fails.
Otherwise, it searches for
.Va modname
in directories set by the
.Va kern.module_path
sysctl variable.
Although modules must have an extension of
.Pa .ko ,
providing extension name is not mandatory, it will be added while searching
for the
.Va modname .
It does not hurt to specify it though.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl r
Extract version information of found objects.
Otherwise print only dependencies.
.It Fl v
Be more verbose when parsing ELF.
.El
.Pp
The kernel file
.Va /boot/kernel/kernel
can also be used as parameter
.Va kernel .
In this case
.Nm
will show all modules builtin into the kernel along with their corresponding
information.
Note, the output can be very excessive.
.Sh FILES
.Va /boot/modules
and
.Va /boot/kernel
are directories containing loadable modules by default.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show info about module by module name, in this case
.Ar iic :
.Pp
.Dl kldinfo iic
.Pp
Show info about module by file name within the module path:
.Pp
.Dl kldinfo iic.ko
.Pp
Show info about module by relative path:
.Pp
.Dl kldinfo ../iic.ko
.Pp
Or by full path:
.Pp
.Dl kldinfo /boot/kernel/iic.ko
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr kldstat 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
